  "subdivision_of_building": "Rear-facing lower ground Floor - single window only, not visible by any others, including as result of high boundary walls.",
  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "Extending the height of the existing rear-facing window downwards by 90cm and replacing with double glazed window, without altering the width or the lintel or other structural amendments. \nThe window is within a ground/lower-ground flat. The window is at the lower-ground level and faces into a courtyard/sunken garden also at the lower-ground level. There is no visual access to the window to anyone else (any other houses, flats, or from the street) as the courtyard garden is sunken and surrounded by high boundary walls as shown on the plans. \nThe building is not listed or in a conservation area. ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;Unless otherwise hereby approved, all new works in respect of all the works hereby approved (and any other incidental works to be carried out in this connection) shall match the existing building in respect of materials used, detailed execution and finished appearance.\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;REASON: To ensure a satisfactory external appearance and safeguard the significance of the locally listed building.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>"
